# The vendored pdf.js is version-pinned by PATH (site/static/pdfjs/) and its
# bytes never change in place, so the /* no-cache default above is pure cost
# for 3.6 MB of renderer on every page load. Long cache, like the covers.
# ⚠️ NOT `immutable`: the path does NOT change when the version does (the
# update procedure overwrites in place — see VENDORED.md), so a lie here would
# strand a browser on an old renderer with no way to correct it.
/static/pdfjs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/dev/static/pdfjs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# The same bargain for viewer phase 2's two vendored drops — foliate-js (10
# modules) and zip.js (44), pinned by COMMIT and by version rather than by path.
# Without this the /* no-cache default costs ~50 conditional requests on every
# load of a page whose renderer bytes never change in place.
# ⚠️ NOT `immutable`, for exactly the pdf.js reason above.
# ⚠️ BOTH LANES, again: `/dev/` is a path, not a host.
/static/foliate/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/dev/static/foliate/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/static/zipjs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/dev/static/zipjs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PLAYER'S CSP — audio player phase 2, 2026-09-02
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /listen is the second page on this origin to want a Content-Security-Policy,
# and it wants one for the same reason /read does: it handles a large binary
# from a CREDENTIALED endpoint, holding a Firebase ID token. The rest of the
# site still ships no CSP.
#
# ⚠️ THIS POLICY IS /read's POLICY PLUS EXACTLY TWO DIRECTIVES, ON PURPOSE.
# The /read string has been exercised in production against real books and its
# every token has a reason written above it. Inventing a fresh policy for a
# page whose first production exercise is also its first exercise ANYWHERE is
# how the estate ate two silent CSP defects already (the missing connect-src
# 'self' that rendered CJK pages as boxes; the missing style-src blob: that
# threw away every typeface the publisher chose). So: copy the proven string,
# add only what audio genuinely needs, and name why each addition is here.
#
#   media-src   ⚠️ THE ONE THAT DECIDES WHETHER ANY SOUND COMES OUT. An
#               <audio src> is governed by media-src, NOT by connect-src, and
#               `default-src 'none'` blocks it. The audio host is named; 'self'
#               is NOT here because nothing on this origin is played.
#               ⚠️ AND NOTE WHAT IS ABSENT: `blob:`. Phase 4 (the PWA) plays
#               offline books from OPFS through `URL.createObjectURL`, which is
#               a blob: URL, and it will need this directive widened. It is
#               left out today because the phase-1b note in the /read block
#               above — "present now so the EPUB build does not have to touch
#               this file" — turned out to be WRONG by exactly two directives,
#               and guessing a future need is what made it wrong. Phase 4 adds
#               it and re-verifies it, which is the only way it is ever known
#               to be right.
#   worker-src  'self' — the bearer-injecting service worker (site/audio-sw.js)
#               is registered from this page, and service-worker registration
#               is governed by worker-src. ⚠️ Blocking it does NOT produce an
#               error the page can act on: registration rejects, no controller
#               ever arrives, every range request goes out bare, and the Worker
#               answers a correct 401 that the media element reports as a bare
#               `error` event with no status. That is the SILENTLY DEAD PLAY
#               BUTTON the whole §3.2 mitigation exists to prevent, arriving
#               through the one door the mitigation does not watch. listen.js
#               words it ("the browser did not start it"), which is the best a
#               page can do about its own missing worker.
#
# Everything else is /read's string verbatim, including the two lines whose
# reasons are written out at length up there and which must not be trimmed
# here without reading them: `connect-src 'self'` (a same-origin fetch is
# blocked by `default-src 'none'` too — this page fetches chapters.json) and
# `frame-ancestors 'self'` (NOT 'none': see the P1 blank-reader incident; this
# page frames no blob: today, but 'self' costs nothing and 'none' is the value
# somebody would "restore for safety" without reading why it was changed).
#
# ⚠️ ALL FOUR RULES, and the reasons are read.html's: `/dev/listen` because the
# dev lane is a PATH and a `/listen` rule does not cover it, and the
# trailing-slash form because Cloudflare 308s and a rule matching only the
# canonical form leaves the redirected request bare. Cloudflare's `*` is a path
# splat, not a glob, so these are spelled out.
#
# 🔴 AND THE HONEST LIMIT, WHICH IS THE SAME ONE THE READER HIT: THIS POLICY
# CANNOT BE EXERCISED ON THE DEV LANE. deploy.yml assembles `_site/` from
# prod-src/site/, so the ROOT `_headers` — the only one Cloudflare reads —
# comes from the PROD branch. Until this file is promoted, /dev/listen ships
# with NO CSP at all and the page will work there whether this string is right
# or wrong. Its FIRST real exercise is production. That is why it is a copy of
# a proven policy plus two named directives rather than a fresh one.
/listen
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' https://www.gstatic.com https://apis.google.com; connect-src 'self' https://audiobook-api.heygabi.ai https://auth.heygabi.ai https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://firestore.googleapis.com https://www.googleapis.com; media-src https://audiobook-api.heygabi.ai; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://covers.heygabi.ai; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; worker-src 'self'; frame-src 'self' https://audiobook-catalog.firebaseapp.com; child-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'

/listen/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' https://www.gstatic.com https://apis.google.com; connect-src 'self' https://audiobook-api.heygabi.ai https://auth.heygabi.ai https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://firestore.googleapis.com https://www.googleapis.com; media-src https://audiobook-api.heygabi.ai; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://covers.heygabi.ai; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; worker-src 'self'; frame-src 'self' https://audiobook-catalog.firebaseapp.com; child-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'

